Sauce Demo – End-to-End Automated Test Suite
A Selenium-based automated test suite that validates the complete online shopping workflow on SauceDemo, from user authentication through to order completion.

📋 Project Overview
This project automates a full e-commerce purchase journey using Selenium WebDriver and TestNG, simulating real user interactions across six sequential test scenarios. It demonstrates practical UI test automation skills applicable to any modern web application.

✅ Test Scenarios Covered

User Login – Authenticates with valid credentials and verifies successful navigation to the product catalogue
Add Item to Cart – Adds a product and confirms the cart badge updates correctly
Navigate to Cart – Opens the cart page and verifies it loads as expected
Initiate Checkout – Proceeds to checkout and confirms the information form is displayed
Enter Customer Information – Fills in shipping details and advances to the order overview
Complete Order – Finalises the purchase and verifies the confirmation message


💡 Concepts Demonstrated

Page Interaction – Locating elements using By.id, By.className, By.xpath, and By.name strategies
Implicit Waits – Configuring global wait timeouts to handle dynamic page loading
Test Ordering & Prioritisation – Using TestNG's @Test(priority = n) to enforce sequential execution of dependent tests
Test Lifecycle Management – Using @BeforeClass and @AfterClass for setup and teardown
Assertions – Validating expected outcomes with Assert.assertEquals and Assert.assertTrue
ChromeOptions Configuration – Suppressing automation banners and browser notifications for cleaner test runs
End-to-End Testing – Simulating a complete user journey across multiple pages and states


🚀 How to Run
bash# Clone the repository
git clone <your-repo-url>

# Run tests via Maven
mvn test

Prerequisites: Java 21+, Maven, and Google Chrome installed. WebDriverManager handles the ChromeDriver setup automatically.
